    bc: Prototype unique heap ownership for measured comparison
    
    Keep three inline limbs while eagerly copying larger vectors, so the
    current COW policy can be compared against unique ownership without
    changing arithmetic or VM algorithms. Copy operations can allocate and
    must not promise noexcept. Preserve independent snapshot values.
    
    This branch is an experiment, not an adoption decision. Adjust only the
    shared-owner count assertions to the experimental representation. All
    212 unit cases (691942 assertions), CLI/VM/arithmetic oracle groups and
    45 quick benchmark oracles pass. Profile owner totals are incomparable;
    measure release timings and process memory before selecting a policy.
    
    Refs #202 and #197.

